    "stem": "一家公司在Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群中运行应用程序。EKS 集群使用Application Load Balancer 将流量路由到运行在集群中的应用程序。一个新迁移到EKS 集群的应用程序性能表现不佳。EKS 集群中的所有其他应用程序都保持适当的运行状态。新应用程序在部署后立即水平扩展到预配置的最大pod 数量，尽管没有任何用户流量路由到该Web 应用程序。哪种解决方案可以解决EKS 集群中Web 应用程序的扩展行为？",
    "stemEn": "A company runs applications in an Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) cluster. The EKS cluster uses an Application Load Balancer to route traffic to the applications that run in the cluster. A new application that was migrated to the EKS cluster is performing poorly. All the other applications in the EKS cluster maintain appropriate operation. The new application scales out horizontally to the preconfigured maximum number of pods immediately upon deployment, before any user traffic routes to the web application. Which solution will resolve the scaling behavior of the web application in the EKS cluster?",
    "stemZh": "一家公司在Amazon Elastic Kubernetes Service (Amazon EKS) 集群中运行应用程序。EKS 集群使用Application Load Balancer 将流量路由到运行在集群中的应用程序。一个新迁移到EKS 集群的应用程序性能表现不佳。EKS 集群中的所有其他应用程序都保持适当的运行状态。新应用程序在部署后立即水平扩展到预配置的最大pod 数量，尽管没有任何用户流量路由到该Web 应用程序。哪种解决方案可以解决EKS 集群中Web 应用程序的扩展行为？",
