    "explanation": "题目分析与解答\n1. 考察的知识点\nAmazon CloudFront的功能，包括Lambda@Edge和CloudFront Functions的使用场景。\n如何实现授权令牌检查以保护资源。\n如何启用CloudWatch日志记录以监控活动。\n如何实现代码的持续部署和更新。\n如何最小化操作复杂性。\n2. 选项分析\nA. Implement an authorization token check in Lambda@Edge as a trigger on the CloudFront distribution. Enable CloudWatch logging for the\nLambda@Edge function. Attach the Lambda@Edge function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.\n正确性分析：Lambda@Edge可以在CloudFront边缘节点执行复杂的逻辑，包括授权令牌检查，并支持CloudWatch日志记录。\n错误性分析：虽然Lambda@Edge功能强大，但其部署和更新过程比CloudFront Functions复杂，操作成本较高，不符合“最小化操作复杂性”的要求。\nB. Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the\nCloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement CloudFront continuous deployment to perform updates.\n正确性分析：CloudFront Functions是专门为轻量级任务设计的，适合实现简单的授权令牌检查。它支持CloudWatch日志记录，并且部署和更新过程非常简单，符合“最小化操作复杂性”的要求。\n错误性分析：无明显错误。\nC. Implement an authorization token check in the application code that is installed on the EC2 instances. Install the CloudWatch agent on the\nEC2 instances. Configure the application to log to the CloudWatch agent. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing.\n正确性分析：可以在EC2实例上实现授权令牌检查，并通过CloudWatch代理记录日志。\n错误性分析：这种方法需要管理EC2实例和应用程序代码，操作复杂性高，不符合“最小化操作复杂性”的要求。此外，使用Route 53加权路由迁移流量增加了额外的复杂性。\nD. Implement an authorization token check in CloudFront Functions. Enable CloudWatch logging for the CloudFront function. Attach the\nCloudFront function to the CloudFront distribution. Implement a second CloudFront distribution. Migrate the traffic from the first CloudFront distribution by using Amazon Route 53 weighted routing.\n正确性分析：CloudFront Functions可以实现授权令牌检查，并支持CloudWatch日志记录。\n错误性分析：引入第二个CloudFront分发和Route 53加权路由增加了额外的复杂性，不符合“最小化操作复杂性”的要求。\n3. 我选的答案\nB\n4. 官方答案\nB\n5. 与官方答案比较\n我的答案与官方答案一致。\n原因：CloudFront Functions是专为轻量级任务设计的，操作复杂性最低，完全满足题目要求。",
    "explanationEn": "",
